# The status checker is zipped by Terraform (archive_file) and deployed by
# source hash. With core.autocrlf, a Windows checkout rewrites it to CRLF and
# Terraform sees "new code" that is not; LF everywhere keeps the hash stable.
status-checker/*.py text eol=lf

# Same failure, other files: Terraform heredocs (e.g. the CloudFront function in
# cache-control.tf) are deployed byte-for-byte, so a CRLF checkout makes every
# plan from Windows want to "update" live code that has not changed.
*.tf text eol=lf
